From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LosDaemons13 <esteveloris@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:42:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs: DM_AMIIBO_DIR in the switches table

The virtual amiibo (hle_sdk16.c) read DM_AMIIBO_DIR, the folder of their
application areas; dm/tools/tests/test_env_switches.py fails on a switch
the code reads that the table does not list.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the table goes with the virtual amiibo patch
Issue: none yet (LosDaemons13/NX2Apple, amiibo in Super Mario Odyssey)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/env_switches.tsv | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 30d63f5..0e47a44 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ DM_AB	diagnostic	`=<frames>` splits the run into phases of that many frames and
 DM_ALIAS_SIZE	diagnostic	`=<bytes>` gives the guest an alias region of that size instead of the platform's, which is at least the Switch's 64 GB on the Mac and the profile's `mem_alias` on an iPhone (at least 256 MB, whole host pages; the heap and stacks stay as they are): the profile's value reproduces an iPhone's address space on the Mac, as the NSP script's heap check does; its address region check sets 64 GB (Mac only: an iPhone has no room)
 DM_ALIAS_WINDOWS	diagnostic	`=<MB>` logs every 30 s how much of each window of that size in the alias region is mapped (windows aligned to their size in absolute addresses)
 DM_ALLOW_OTHER_METAL	switch	`1` lets `own_compilers.py` build the shader libraries with a Metal compiler other than the one in `dmsh_chain.lock` (it stops otherwise, GitHub issue #242); the NSP script sets it for `--allow-other-metal`
+DM_AMIIBO_DIR	path	Folder where the virtual amiibo keep their application areas (`hle_sdk16.c`, nfp): `<amiibo ID>/<access ID>.bin`, so one amiibo holds an area for each game that used it; by default an `amiibo` folder beside `DM_SAVE`, and NX2Apple's shell sets `Documents/amiibo`
 DM_AOC_DIR	path	Folder of add-on content: one numbered subfolder per DLC index holding that DLC's RomFS, reported by `aoc` and mounted read-only; the app, the Mac launcher and the NSP script set it when the build has DLC
 DM_AOC_OWNED	switch	`0` reports no add-on content even when `DM_AOC_DIR` has some, for runs without the DLC
 DM_APP_DM	path	Set by the iOS app of a game of several programs: the running program's `dm/p<N>` folder, where the settings screen finds its `launcher.json`
